\pard\intbl\cell *: Do I espy a wand'rer come to visit? I bid thee welcome, friend. Now, unless mine eyes deceive me, thou art no callow youth, but rather a seasoned warrior.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1722\cellx10333 
\pard\intbl\cell *: Allow me to apprise thee of what hath befallen this place\emdash 'twas once the fair town of Damdara. Alas, 'tis now a monster-ravaged wasteland whose people have all fled.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1722\cellx10333 
\pard\intbl\cell *: Our woes began when marauding fiends laid waste to our beloved home. Now one among them is risen again\emdash by what foul means I know not. I speak of that shadowy chevalier, the knight aberrant.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1722\cellx10333 
\pard\intbl\cell *: This wicked being now ruleth o'er the ruins of Damdara, and hath roused the departed from their slumber that he might tyrannise them. ...Yea, I myself am one such unfortunate soul.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1722\cellx10333 
\pard\intbl\cell *: I know not who thou art, friend, but I beseech thee\emdash take up arms against the knight aberrant and return us to our rest! Prithee, banish the darkness that hath descended upon this place!\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1722\cellx10333 
\pard\intbl\cell You've been asked to undertake a quest.<LM_LF>Will you acquiesce to this request?\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1722\cellx10333 
\pard\intbl\cell *: I would not presume to grovel, wand'rer, but wilt thou perchance reconsider? None but a seasoned warrior such as thyself can bring this nightmare to an end, I fear...\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1722\cellx10333 
\pard\intbl\cell *: Huzzah! Thou wilt accede to my request? Verily, the hero we have awaited hath come at last! Now\emdash thine enemy, the knight aberrant, doth oft appear behind the armourer's in the south-east of the town.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1722\cellx10333 
\pard\intbl\cell *: Prithee, lay this foul fiend to rest, that our own unquiet souls may sleep in peace once more.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1722\cellx10333 
\pard\intbl\cell *: The knight aberrant\emdash the foul fiend under whose yoke we slaveth\emdash doth oft appear behind the armourer in the south-east of the town.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1722\cellx10333 
\pard\intbl\cell *: Prithee, lay the foul fiend to rest, that our own unquiet souls may sleep in peace once more.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1722\cellx10333 
\pard\intbl\cell *: Praise be! We are delivered from our plight! Verily, thou art the saviour we have so long awaited!\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1722\cellx10333 
\pard\intbl\cell *: Prithee, accept this small token of my gratitude, trifling though it be.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1722\cellx10333 
\pard\intbl\cell *: Hadst thou not happened upon our humble town, mayhap we might never have been saved. Now though, thanks to thy timely intervention, we may sleep peacefully at last.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1722\cellx10333 
\pard\intbl\cell *: I am Galen, best among bards, whose praises once were sung in every corner of this fair land.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1722\cellx10333 
\pard\intbl Galen\cell The town of Damdara, in whose ruins thou standest, was once a bustling and handsome settlement. But alas, no more...\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1722\cellx10333 
\pard\intbl Galen\cell Though when I close mine eyes, glad scenes of yesteryear do float before me as if they occurred only yesterday. Come friend, join me in my reverie...\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1722\cellx10333 
\pard\intbl\cell *: The monstrous marauders didst fall upon our town as a lion doth its prey. Those who could not flee in time were slain without mercy.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1722\cellx10333 
\pard\intbl\cell *: Aye, 'tis true\emdash all those thou wilt encounter here are long since dead. Yet all were rudely roused from their slumber, and now haunt the very place they once called home.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1722\cellx10333 
\pard\intbl\cell *: Awoken by the knight aberrant, that he might terrorise what remaineth of this place all the more. Truly, our fate is not one that I would wish upon my most bitter foe...\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1722\cellx10333 
\pard\intbl\cell *: Hadst thou come sooner, thou wouldst have found all manner of fine items available to purchase. Alas, we have been forced to offer up all that we own to that wicked tyrant, the knight aberrant.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1722\cellx10333 
\pard\intbl\cell *: Fie upon him! Would it not have sufficed to rob us of our lives!? Wherefore must the fiend torment us even beyond the grave? Verily, fate is a cruel mistress indeed...\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1722\cellx10333 
\pard\intbl\cell *: Our heartless new master brooketh no dissent. Were we to display the merest hint of resistance, we would doubtless be cruelly punished.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1722\cellx10333 
\pard\intbl\cell *: Yet we are safe for the nonce\emdash the wicked creature is abroad. 'Pon his return, he will no doubt resume his favoured post behind Magog's shop o'er yonder...\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1722\cellx10333 
\pard\intbl\cell *: In days of yore, these were the premises of a dear companion\emdash Magog the armourer.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1722\cellx10333 
\pard\intbl\cell *: 'Tis reason to give thanks indeed that he and his kin did flee the town ere the monsters destroyed it.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1722\cellx10333 
\pard\intbl\cell *: Would that I had been so wise... Alas, I was cut down where I stood, and now have little choice but to serve as the vassal of our vile oppressor.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1722\cellx10333 
\pard\intbl\cell *: Lo, might this be our saviour who standeth before me? Might this be the one to smite the knight aberrant and free us from his cruel vassalage at last?\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1722\cellx10333 
\pard\intbl\cell *: Our tormentor doth oft appear behind this place. Gird up thy loins, friend, and do thine utmost to end our suffering!\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1722\cellx10333 
\pard\intbl\cell *: How long has it been since the town fell to the fiends and our servitude began? Verily, 'tis too painful to dwell upon it...\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1722\cellx10333 
\pard\intbl\cell *: Yea, to lose one's life is a fate cruel enough in itself\emdash to lose one's honour and bow to the will of monsters...this, truly, is a fate worse than death...\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1722\cellx10333 
\pard\intbl\cell *: There is no rest for we unhappy souls... Trapped 'twixt life and death, we toil morning, noon and night... How I long for release... How I long to know peace at last...\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1722\cellx10333 
\pard\intbl\cell *: Yet 'tis hopeless, it seems... Our cruel master hath sentenced us to ceaseless servitude...\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1722\cellx10333 
\pard\intbl\cell *: A curious memory doth trouble my mind of late. I didst espy Magog as he buried a certain something 'neath the tree behind his shop. 'Twas on the very eve of the calamity that struck us.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1722\cellx10333 
\pard\intbl\cell *: Though what it might have been, I know not. And besides, 'twas long ago\emdash whate'er it was has doubtless long since been disinterred or otherwise removed...\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1722\cellx10333 
\pard\intbl\cell *: This place was once an inn. Alas, it was long since left to crumble. It paineth me to say it, but nary a bed remaineth where a weary traveller might lay his head.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1722\cellx10333 
\pard\intbl\cell *: Alack, 'tis a fate worse than death to see it so depleted! Though that particular fate hath long since befallen me...\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1722\cellx10333 
\pard\intbl\cell *: Heed me, wanderer: the knight aberrant under whose tyranny we labour is known to appear without warning to the rear of the armourer's shop. Be sure to be on thy guard!\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1722\cellx10333 
\pard\intbl\cell *: As to the matter of wherefore he might haunt such a place, this I know not. Could something precious perhaps have been lost to him there...?\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1722\cellx10333 
\pard\intbl Alena\cell Yoy! This heat is too much powerful! It makes everyone exhausted completely.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1722\cellx10333 
\pard\intbl Alena\cell But I am incapable to abandon my quest regardless. And so, I create an adventurer's band with these fellows. I begin to consider that this was perhaps not an act of genius...\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
